<https://example.org/maintenance/evidence/bd5aabae7d89f217e55defb2/0> a maint:Evidence ;
    maint:page 54 ;
    maint:quote "Excessive moisture causes failures in motor winding insulation" ;
    maint:sourceJSON "{\"bbox\": [62.63999557495117, 426.9633483886719, 510.0133361816406, 463.6756591796875], \"clean_end\": 82, \"clean_start\": 20, \"document_id\": \"DOC_cf0bdf9d28720ead73ea3680ce4f0d19dc8ff2f84bcf454378dea1215b51fa22\", \"document_name\": \"NP_7502_Electric Motor Predictive and Preventive Maintenance Guide.pdf\", \"original_end\": 82, \"original_quote\": \"Excessive moisture causes failures in motor winding insulation\", \"original_start\": 20, \"page\": 54, \"paragraph_id\": \"P54_B6\", \"quote\": \"Excessive moisture causes failures in motor winding insulation\", \"section\": \"Moisture and motor insulation\", \"section_id\": \"epri-moisture\", \"source_paragraph_cleaned\": \"Excessive Moisture. Excessive moisture causes failures in motor winding insulation and in motor leads. It can also cause loss of lubrication capability in bearing oil systems and deterioration of motor parts, both electrical and mechanical.\", \"source_paragraph_original\": \"Excessive Moisture. Excessive moisture causes failures in motor winding insulation and\\nin motor leads. It can also cause loss of lubrication capability in bearing oil systems and\\ndeterioration of motor parts, both electrical and mechanical.\\n\"}" .

<https://example.org/maintenance/evidence/bef6647b0157f3bafe0e7662/0> a maint:Evidence ;
    maint:page 6 ;
    maint:quote "A heavier load than designed for" ;
    maint:sourceJSON "{\"bbox\": [268.7143249511719, 393.11505126953125, 542.9324951171875, 576.4556274414062], \"clean_end\": 217, \"clean_start\": 185, \"document_id\": \"DOC_bc4bdf2b43eb7832b16dfab1668af3e742a93a1cb1dbfd36ba2b901d5af6a371\", \"document_name\": \"13-common-causes.pdf\", \"original_end\": 222, \"original_quote\": \"A heavier load than designed for\", \"original_start\": 190, \"page\": 6, \"paragraph_id\": \"P6_B5\", \"quote\": \"A heavier load than designed for\", \"section\": \"10 Bearing wear\", \"section_id\": \"fault-10\", \"source_paragraph_cleaned\": \"A failed bearing has increased drag, emits more heat, and has lower efficiency because of a mechanical, lubrication, or wear problem. Bearing failure can be caused by several things: • A heavier load than designed for • Inadequate or incorrect lubrication • Ineffective bearing sealing • Shaft misalignment • Incorrect fit • Normal wear • Induced shaft voltages Once bearing failure begins, it also creates a cascade effect that accelerates motor failure. 13 % of motor failures are caused by bearing failure, and more than 60 % of the mechanical failures in a facility are caused by bearing wear, so learning how to troubleshoot this potential problem is important.\", \"source_paragraph_original\": \"A failed bearing has increased drag, emits more heat, and has \\nlower efficiency because of a mechanical, lubrication, or wear  \\nproblem. Bearing failure can be caused by several things: \\n•\\t A heavier load than designed for\\n•\\t Inadequate or incorrect lubrication\\n•\\t Ineffective bearing sealing\\n•\\t Shaft misalignment \\n•\\t Incorrect fit\\n•\\t Normal wear\\n•\\t Induced shaft voltages\\nOnce bearing failure begins, it also creates a cascade effect that \\naccelerates motor failure. 13 % of motor failures are caused by  \\nbearing failure, and more than 60 % of the mechanical failures  \\nin a facility are caused by bearing wear, so learning how to \\ntroubleshoot this potential problem is important. \\n\"}" .

<https://example.org/maintenance/evidence/bf9b48893740bf3fa357d453/0> a maint:Evidence ;
    maint:page 54 ;
    maint:quote "and deterioration of motor parts, both electrical and mechanical" ;
    maint:sourceJSON "{\"bbox\": [62.63999557495117, 426.9633483886719, 510.0133361816406, 463.6756591796875], \"clean_end\": 239, \"clean_start\": 175, \"document_id\": \"DOC_cf0bdf9d28720ead73ea3680ce4f0d19dc8ff2f84bcf454378dea1215b51fa22\", \"document_name\": \"NP_7502_Electric Motor Predictive and Preventive Maintenance Guide.pdf\", \"original_end\": 239, \"original_quote\": \"and\\ndeterioration of motor parts, both electrical and mechanical\", \"original_start\": 175, \"page\": 54, \"paragraph_id\": \"P54_B6\", \"quote\": \"and deterioration of motor parts, both electrical and mechanical\", \"section\": \"Moisture and motor insulation\", \"section_id\": \"epri-moisture\", \"source_paragraph_cleaned\": \"Excessive Moisture. Excessive moisture causes failures in motor winding insulation and in motor leads. It can also cause loss of lubrication capability in bearing oil systems and deterioration of motor parts, both electrical and mechanical.\", \"source_paragraph_original\": \"Excessive Moisture. Excessive moisture causes failures in motor winding insulation and\\nin motor leads. It can also cause loss of lubrication capability in bearing oil systems and\\ndeterioration of motor parts, both electrical and mechanical.\\n\"}" .

<https://example.org/maintenance/evidence/c5f8a671348ae93ec72c75bf/0> a maint:Evidence ;
    maint:page 25 ;
    maint:quote "Ensure the rating plate voltage is maintained. Check connection." ;
    maint:sourceJSON "{\"bbox\": [211.87811279296875, 559.7347412109375, 530.62890625, 577.3117065429688], \"clean_end\": 76, \"clean_start\": 12, \"document_id\": \"DOC_90dca734e4b5699ff37901e18cdb90275e77ded8b355359130c493820d2fa913\", \"document_name\": \"3GZF500730-85 RevH_EN 06-2022_lowres.pdf\", \"original_end\": 77, \"original_quote\": \"Ensure the rating plate voltage is maintained. \\nCheck connection.\", \"original_start\": 12, \"page\": 25, \"paragraph_id\": \"P25_B19\", \"quote\": \"Ensure the rating plate voltage is maintained. Check connection.\", \"section\": \"Motor stalls\", \"section_id\": \"abb-stalls\", \"source_paragraph_cleaned\": \"Low voltage Ensure the rating plate voltage is maintained. Check connection.\", \"source_paragraph_original\": \"Low voltage\\nEnsure the rating plate voltage is maintained. \\nCheck connection.\\n\"}" .

<https://example.org/maintenance/evidence/cf543ea5b4489c9001c917ac/0> a maint:Evidence ;
    maint:page 12 ;
    maint:quote "Light rust or corrosion should be removed with emery paper (240 – 320 # grit)." ;
    maint:sourceJSON "{\"bbox\": [308.99884033203125, 269.972412109375, 560.1600341796875, 320.7309265136719], \"clean_end\": 78, \"clean_start\": 0, \"document_id\": \"DOC_eae8090d19d0478c75eda61af9c97af5953dc4395b339ef3c9806d9fa405e1ad\", \"document_name\": \"Manual_Udrzba_Montaz_TIMKEN_AJ.pdf\", \"original_end\": 79, \"original_quote\": \"Light rust or corrosion should be removed with emery paper \\n(240 – 320 # grit).\", \"original_start\": 0, \"page\": 12, \"paragraph_id\": \"P12_B6\", \"quote\": \"Light rust or corrosion should be removed with emery paper (240 – 320 # grit).\", \"section\": \"Bearing repair\", \"section_id\": \"timken-repair\", \"source_paragraph_cleaned\": \"Light rust or corrosion should be removed with emery paper (240 – 320 # grit). As much of the damage should be removed as possible to prevent it from contaminating the bearing when it is returned to service.\", \"source_paragraph_original\": \"Light rust or corrosion should be removed with emery paper \\n(240 – 320 # grit). As much of the damage should be removed as \\npossible to prevent it from contaminating the bearing when it is \\nreturned to service.\\n\"}" .

<https://example.org/maintenance/evidence/cfe1edb8b29d288904fa84c8/0> a maint:Evidence ;
    maint:page 12 ;
    maint:quote "may still be returned to service after repair or refurbishment" ;
    maint:sourceJSON "{\"bbox\": [41.99760055541992, 601.0715942382812, 293.1300964355469, 690.818115234375], \"clean_end\": 274, \"clean_start\": 212, \"document_id\": \"DOC_eae8090d19d0478c75eda61af9c97af5953dc4395b339ef3c9806d9fa405e1ad\", \"document_name\": \"Manual_Udrzba_Montaz_TIMKEN_AJ.pdf\", \"original_end\": 277, \"original_quote\": \"may still be returned to service after \\nrepair or refurbishment\", \"original_start\": 214, \"page\": 12, \"paragraph_id\": \"P12_B24\", \"quote\": \"may still be returned to service after repair or refurbishment\", \"section\": \"Damaged bearings\", \"section_id\": \"timken-damage\", \"source_paragraph_cleaned\": \"Despite taking proper precautions, bearings may become dam- aged either through improper storage and handling or through normal wear in use. Bearings that have been damaged or are no longer within specifications may still be returned to service after repair or refurbishment. Some bearings can be refurbished more than once. Eventually all bearings will sustain sufficient wear or damage and will have to be replaced.\", \"source_paragraph_original\": \"Despite taking proper precautions, bearings may become dam-\\naged either through improper storage and handling or through \\nnormal wear in use. Bearings that have been damaged or are no \\nlonger within specifications may still be returned to service after \\nrepair or refurbishment. Some bearings can be refurbished more \\nthan once. Eventually all bearings will sustain sufficient wear or \\ndamage and will have to be replaced.\\n\"}" .

<https://example.org/maintenance/evidence/d53546437e969abd2936db93/0> a maint:Evidence ;
    maint:page 2 ;
    maint:quote "that then increases operating temperatures" ;
    maint:sourceJSON "{\"bbox\": [268.71429443359375, 523.3394165039062, 547.9678344726562, 556.6939086914062], \"clean_end\": 113, \"clean_start\": 71, \"document_id\": \"DOC_bc4bdf2b43eb7832b16dfab1668af3e742a93a1cb1dbfd36ba2b901d5af6a371\", \"document_name\": \"13-common-causes.pdf\", \"original_end\": 114, \"original_quote\": \"that then increases operating temperatures\", \"original_start\": 72, \"page\": 2, \"paragraph_id\": \"P2_B6\", \"quote\": \"that then increases operating temperatures\", \"section\": \"2 Voltage imbalance\", \"section_id\": \"fault-02\", \"source_paragraph_cleaned\": \"Impact: Imbalance creates excessive current flow in one or more phases that then increases operating temperatures–leading to insulation breakdown\", \"source_paragraph_original\": \"Impact: Imbalance creates excessive current flow in one or more \\nphases that then increases operating temperatures–leading to  \\ninsulation breakdown\\n\"}" .

<https://example.org/maintenance/evidence/ddfce40be3e2af62db650fe2/0> a maint:Evidence ;
    maint:page 6 ;
    maint:quote "Ineffective bearing sealing" ;
    maint:sourceJSON "{\"bbox\": [268.7143249511719, 393.11505126953125, 542.9324951171875, 576.4556274414062], \"clean_end\": 285, \"clean_start\": 258, \"document_id\": \"DOC_bc4bdf2b43eb7832b16dfab1668af3e742a93a1cb1dbfd36ba2b901d5af6a371\", \"document_name\": \"13-common-causes.pdf\", \"original_end\": 292, \"original_quote\": \"Ineffective bearing sealing\", \"original_start\": 265, \"page\": 6, \"paragraph_id\": \"P6_B5\", \"quote\": \"Ineffective bearing sealing\", \"section\": \"10 Bearing wear\", \"section_id\": \"fault-10\", \"source_paragraph_cleaned\": \"A failed bearing has increased drag, emits more heat, and has lower efficiency because of a mechanical, lubrication, or wear problem. Bearing failure can be caused by several things: • A heavier load than designed for • Inadequate or incorrect lubrication • Ineffective bearing sealing • Shaft misalignment • Incorrect fit • Normal wear • Induced shaft voltages Once bearing failure begins, it also creates a cascade effect that accelerates motor failure. 13 % of motor failures are caused by bearing failure, and more than 60 % of the mechanical failures in a facility are caused by bearing wear, so learning how to troubleshoot this potential problem is important.\", \"source_paragraph_original\": \"A failed bearing has increased drag, emits more heat, and has \\nlower efficiency because of a mechanical, lubrication, or wear  \\nproblem. Bearing failure can be caused by several things: \\n•\\t A heavier load than designed for\\n•\\t Inadequate or incorrect lubrication\\n•\\t Ineffective bearing sealing\\n•\\t Shaft misalignment \\n•\\t Incorrect fit\\n•\\t Normal wear\\n•\\t Induced shaft voltages\\nOnce bearing failure begins, it also creates a cascade effect that \\naccelerates motor failure. 13 % of motor failures are caused by  \\nbearing failure, and more than 60 % of the mechanical failures  \\nin a facility are caused by bearing wear, so learning how to \\ntroubleshoot this potential problem is important. \\n\"}" .

